          <mxGeometry x="310" y="3500" width="204" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="IY0VTX6cTRXR3Q0A2DRt-40" value="&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;APi Stores the request in form of yaml in tis cache&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Other components are listening to the Api Server&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Scheduler sees here is an yaml file with workernode is blank&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Scheduler decides which worker nodes , It checks which worker node is running and which worker node has resources available&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Scheduler put the entry of the worker node its work is done&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Now kubelet comes in to the picture , kubelet is the client service, also listening to the APi Server continuously&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Kubelet check there is a request of creating a pod in the cache having workernode =w2&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;kubelet of W2 see its request for me&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;kubelet service pull the request&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;creates a Pod inside the W2&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;kubelet calling to the CRI in the backend&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;CRI creates a Container inside the Pod&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Pod willl get the IP address from the subnet of the W2 private network&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;kubelet update the pod Ip and staus to the yaml file (Api server)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Its the meta data of the Pod , actual pod is running in W2&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;apiServer calling to the etcd in the backend and ensure this metadata store in the etcd database.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;If master node rebooted , api will fetch the data back from the etcd, there is no impact on the Pod because its running on the W2&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;If master down we can&#39;t do any operation changes , but there is no impact on exsisting running Pod&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;If W2 go offiline then what happen to the Pod running inside W2&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Here controller manager comes in the picture , recreate the Pod in another node&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;Want to rollingUpdate&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Scale&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Fault Tolerance&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Provide HA (same application in to two pods)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;controller-manager update the yaml&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;all the service communication also happen through apiServer&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;kube-proxy:&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;communication service&amp;nbsp; outside the world- access application running inside the pod&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;allow any application IOPS operation&amp;nbsp; from the external world www....&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="3800" width="750" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
